OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,FThe UK will see its fullest solar
OL,7,Feclipse for the next 54 years on
OL,8,FWednesday.
OL,10,FMore than 90% of the Sun will be
OL,11,Fobscured by the Moon between 6.17pm
OL,12,Fand 8.06pm on August 12, the most it
OL,13,Fhas been blocked above UK skies since
OL,14,Fthe total eclipse in 1999.
OL,16,FExperts from the Royal Greenwich
OL,17,FObservatory have warned the public
OL,18,Fthat "can't just go out and expect to
OL,19,Fhave a look as this is dangerous for
OL,20,Fthe eyes".
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
