OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,FWhy is looking at a solar eclipse
OL,7,Fdangerous?
OL,9,FEye damage can occur without proper
OL,10,Fprotection. The sun's bright rays can
OL,11,Fburn cells in the retina at the back
OL,12,Fof the eye.
OL,14,FThe retina doesn't have pain
OL,15,Freceptors, so there's no way to feel
OL,16,Fthe damage as it happens. Once the
OL,17,Fcells die, they don't come back.
OL,19,FSymptoms of solar eye damage, called
OL,20,Fsolar retinopathy, include blurred
OL,21,Fvision and colour distortion.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
