OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F311A1786475919
OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,FThere's no set rule for how long of a
OL,7,Fglance can lead to permanent damage.
OL,8,FSeverity varies based on cloudiness,
OL,9,Fair pollution and a person's vantage
OL,10,Fpoint.
OL,12,FBut doctors say looking at a solar
OL,13,Feclipse for even a few seconds
OL,14,Funprotected isn't worth the risk.
OL,16,FHow can you watch it safely?
OL,18,FBell, a planetarium astronomer at the
OL,19,FRGO, said it is important to come
OL,20,Fprepared to watch the solar eclipse on
OL,21,FWednesday.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
