OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,F"You can use solar eclipse glasses,
OL,7,Fwhich are very, very different from
OL,8,Fsunglasses ` they block out so much
OL,9,Flight that you can't see anything
OL,10,Fthrough them except the Sun, because
OL,11,Fthat's how much light they need to
OL,12,Fblock for the damaging light of the
OL,13,FSun to be safe to view.
OL,15,F"Ideally a solar telescope is an
OL,16,Famazing way to witness it, and if you
OL,17,Fdon't have one of them then you can
OL,18,Flook into whether your local astronomy
OL,19,Fsociety is doing any events.
OL,26,@wD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
