OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F311A1786475919
OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,F"And if all else fails, you can
OL,7,Fproject the image of the eclipse using
OL,8,Fa household item like a colander which
OL,9,Fhas lots of holes in ` point the
OL,10,Fcolander towards the Sun with your
OL,11,Fback facing it, and in the shadow of
OL,12,Fthe colander you'll be able to see the
OL,13,Feclipse in the holes, which is really
OL,14,Fcool."
OL,16,FMohamed Elalfy, a consultant
OL,17,Fophthalmologist and president of the
OL,18,FRoyal College of Ophthalmologists,
OL,19,Fsaid: "The safest way to enjoy the
OL,20,Feclipse is to observe it indirectly,
OL,21,Fsuch as by watching a live broadcast.
OL,26,@nD@AOUvD@FO]{D@GOU
