OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,F"Looking directly at the Sun during a
OL,7,Fsolar eclipse can cause damage to the
OL,8,Fretina, potentially damaging the cells
OL,9,Fresponsible for sharp central vision."
OL,11,FExperts have warned that only special
OL,12,Fsolar eclipse glasses that are ISO
OL,13,F12312-2 certified for the safest eye
OL,14,Fprotection should be used to view the
OL,15,Feclipse.
OL,17,FHowever, they have all but sold out
OL,18,Fonline ahead of the event, or carry
OL,19,Fhefty delivery fees to arrive in time.
OL,26,@nD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
