CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F311A1786475919
OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,FExperts have warned that so-called
OL,7,Feclipse glasses that do not carry the
OL,8,Fsafety standards, or ordinary
OL,9,Fsunglasses, no matter how dark, should
OL,10,Fnever be worn to view an eclipse, as
OL,11,Fthey reduce glare, making it feel more
OL,12,Fcomfortable to look at the Sun for
OL,13,Flonger, but still allow harmful solar
OL,14,Fradiation to reach the retina.
OL,16,FKyla Black, Boots Opticians director
OL,17,Fof optical practice, urged parents to
OL,18,Fbe "particularly careful" letting
OL,19,Ftheir children view the eclipse, and
OL,20,Fwarned some DIY filters can also be
OL,21,Fdangerous.
OL,26,@zD@DOUzD@YO]
